    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **66 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` read-time-derived pattern:\n\n1. **New function step** \u2014 `MarkCityCapacityWarning.java`: counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-trimmed, exactly matching the hard-limit rule's `normalize`/`findAll()` logic) and sets `capacityWarning = true` when the count is in `[40, 49]` \u2014 i.e. `count >= 40 && count < CheckOwnerCityCapacity.CAPACITY` (50). It reuses the existing `CAPACITY` constant so the warning stays tied to the hard limit.\n\n2. **Model** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean capacityWarning` field with getter/setter to `Owner.java` (mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`; MapStruct maps it onto the DTO automatically by name, so no mapper change).\n\n3. **OpenAPI schema** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the Owner schema in `openapi.yml` so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n4. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted the `capacityWarning` step right after `bulkWarning` in both `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml` (`readonly-transaction`) and `owners.POST.yml` (`transaction`), so the flag is recomputed at read time and returned consistently on GET and create.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 (`CheckOwnerCityCapacity` \u2192 409) is untouched. The new `Cp54Tests` passes, as do the existing capacity (`Cp18`) and bulk-warning (`Cp22`) tests and the full suite.\n\nNote: like the existing per-city and per-day rules, this counts via `OwnerRepository.findAll()` in memory rather than a SQL count \u2014 I kept it identical to the established pattern rather than introducing a new query.",
